cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CorpusSLR, please cite it."
title: "CorpusSLR: from one structured query to a PRISMA-documented corpus"
authors:
  - family-names: "Matysik"
    given-names: "Sebastian"
    affiliation: "University of Szczecin, Institute of Management, Doctoral School, Szczecin, Poland"
    email: "sebastian.matysik@usz.edu.pl"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-matysik/CorpusSLR"
abstract: >-
  CorpusSLR automates the identification phase of systematic literature reviews.
  One structured query is compiled to the native syntax of multiple
  bibliographic databases, records from APIs and file exports are harmonized and
  enriched, duplicates are removed by a cascading auditable procedure, and the
  PRISMA 2020 flow diagram together with the PRISMA-S search-reporting appendix
  is generated from the recorded audit trail.
keywords: [systematic literature review, PRISMA, PRISMA-S, deduplication, Scopus,
           OpenAlex, PubMed, Crossref, Semantic Scholar, arXiv, Embase, EBSCOhost,
           ProQuest, RIS, BibTeX, EndNote, evidence synthesis, meta-research]
